1
00:04:45,600 --> 00:04:51,600
He was the perfect weapon until he became the target.

2
00:09:31,200 --> 00:09:37,200
The Bourne Identity is a action, drama, mystery film directed by Doug Liman.

3
00:14:16,800 --> 00:14:22,800
Wounded to the brink of death and suffering from amnesia,
Jason Bourne is rescued at sea by a fisherman.

4
00:19:02,400 --> 00:19:08,400
With nothing to go on but a Swiss bank account number, he starts to reconstruct
his life, but finds that many people he encounters want him dead.

5
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:54,000
However, Bourne realizes that he has the combat and mental skills
of a world-class spy—but who does he work for?

6
00:28:33,600 --> 00:28:39,600
Jason Bourne, played by Matt Damon.

7
00:33:19,200 --> 00:33:25,200
Marie Helena Kreutz, played by Franka Potente.

8
00:38:04,800 --> 00:38:10,800
Alexander Conklin, played by Chris Cooper.

9
00:42:50,400 --> 00:42:56,400
The Professor, played by Clive Owen.

10
00:47:36,000 --> 00:47:42,000
Ward Abbott, played by Brian Cox.

11
00:52:21,600 --> 00:52:27,600
Nykwana Wombosi, played by Adewale Akinnuoye-Agbaje.

12
00:57:07,200 --> 00:57:13,200
The Bourne Identity is a 2002 American action-thriller film directed by Doug
Liman and written by Tony Gilroy and William Blake Herron.

13
01:01:52,800 --> 01:01:58,800
Based on Robert Ludlum's 1980 novel of the same name, it is the first installment in the Bourne franchise, and the film
stars Matt Damon, Franka Potente, Chris Cooper, Clive Owen, Brian Cox, and Adewale Akinnuoye-Agbaje.

14
01:06:38,400 --> 01:06:44,400
In the film, Jason Bourne (Damon) suffers from psychogenic amnesia and is forced to
fight to unlock his identity and his mysterious connection to the CIA.

15
01:11:24,000 --> 01:11:30,000
Attempts to develop a feature film adaptation of Ludlum's novel first began in 1981 but
stalled after being passed to different distributors, with Warner Bros.

16
01:16:09,600 --> 01:16:15,600
producing a television film adaptation in 1988.

17
01:20:55,200 --> 01:21:01,200
Liman revived the feature film project in 1996 and worked with Ludlum and David Self on its screenplay after Gilroy initially
declined: Gilroy made several changes to the script upon joining, with additional contributions from Herron.

18
01:25:40,800 --> 01:25:46,800
After Damon and Potente were cast, principal photography began in October 2000 and lasted until February
2001, with filming taking place in Paris, Prague, Imperia, Rome, Mykonos, and Zürich.

19
01:30:26,400 --> 01:30:32,400
Production was troubled: the creators frequently clashed with studio executives
over delays, costs, last-minute changes, and unexpected reshoots.

20
01:35:12,000 --> 01:35:18,000
Originally set for release in September 2001, it was theatrically released in
the United States on June 14, 2002, by Universal Pictures.

21
01:39:57,600 --> 01:40:03,600
The film received positive reviews from critics, with praise for the direction, Damon's performance, action
sequences, and characters: it is considered one of the most influential action films of all time.

22
01:44:43,200 --> 01:44:49,200
It grossed $214 million worldwide and was followed by the sequels The Bourne Supremacy (2004),
The Bourne Ultimatum (2007), The Bourne Legacy (2012) and Jason Bourne (2016).

23
01:49:28,800 --> 01:49:34,800
The film explores themes of sniper, assassin, amnesia,
paris, france, based on novel or book.

24
01:54:14,400 --> 01:54:20,400
The tone is mind_bending and emotional and intense.
